WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.585
Adaptive support can compensate for model
mismatch while the vehicle operates.

00:00:04.585 --> 00:00:09.031
The next question is whether the system
can learn a reusable description of

00:00:09.031 --> 00:00:09.937
that mismatch.

00:00:09.937 --> 00:00:13.699
The objective is to improve prediction and
reduce reliance on continuous

00:00:13.699 --> 00:00:17.000
adaptive compensation, rather than claim
an unmeasured energy saving.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.196
Model predictive control uses linearized
dynamics to predict the vehicle

00:00:22.196 --> 00:00:22.790
response.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.901
Measurements reveal effects that this
nominal model misses.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:29.497
The gap between predicted and observed
dynamics supplies information for

00:00:29.497 --> 00:00:30.091
learning.

00:00:30.091 --> 00:00:34.407
The network aims to describe that
residual, rather than replace the entire

00:00:34.407 --> 00:00:35.000
controller.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.655
Initially, adaptive reference management
and predictive control operate

00:00:39.655 --> 00:00:40.285
together.

00:00:40.285 --> 00:00:44.103
As the underwater vehicle follows
commands, measurements and applied inputs

00:00:44.103 --> 00:00:45.497
provide learning data.

00:00:45.497 --> 00:00:49.697
The adaptive layer remains active during
this stage, helping control the

00:00:49.697 --> 00:00:53.000
vehicle while the network learns from its
experience.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.269
The learning network estimates a
correction to the nominal dynamics.

00:00:58.269 --> 00:01:01.939
That correction is intended for use inside
the predictive model.

00:01:01.939 --> 00:01:05.953
It is not a separate actuator command
added to the output.

00:01:05.953 --> 00:01:10.087
The scene shows the intended reduction of
model mismatch, not a measured

00:01:10.087 --> 00:01:11.000
training curve.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.728
Learning alone is not enough to justify a
handover.

00:01:15.728 --> 00:01:19.617
The correction must be checked on relevant
conditions, and its effect on

00:01:19.617 --> 00:01:21.772
tracking and constraints must be assessed.

00:01:21.772 --> 00:01:25.224
Adaptive support stays available until
those checks justify the transition.

00:01:25.224 --> 00:01:29.000
A training loss by itself is not proof of
closed-loop reliability.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.701
After validation, the intended transition
disables the adaptive reference

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:34.269
contribution.

00:01:34.269 --> 00:01:37.594
The learned dynamics correction remains
inside model predictive control.

00:01:37.594 --> 00:01:40.574
The optimization structure and actuator
limits are retained.

00:01:40.574 --> 00:01:45.053
This is the research handover being
investigated, not a claim that the network

00:01:45.053 --> 00:01:47.000
has learned every possible condition.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.348
A new depth and heading command tests the
post-handover configuration.

00:01:52.348 --> 00:01:56.096
Predictive control uses the nominal model
plus the learned correction.

00:01:56.096 --> 00:01:59.264
Tracking, constraint compliance, and
sensitivity to unfamiliar conditions must

00:01:59.264 --> 00:02:00.548
all be evaluated.

00:02:00.548 --> 00:02:04.419
The motion here illustrates the intended
behavior rather than a validated

00:02:04.419 --> 00:02:05.000
experiment.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.526
The expected value is retained model
knowledge and less dependence on

00:02:10.526 --> 00:02:12.899
continuous adaptive correction within
validated conditions.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:16.469
Whether this also saves computation or
electrical energy requires measurement:

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.913
network inference and optimization have
costs of their own.

00:02:19.913 --> 00:02:23.000
This project remains a research concept
under development.
